<title>POLAND: SHARE OF FOOD SPENDING FALLS IN POLISH CPI BASKET.</title>
<headline>SHARE OF FOOD SPENDING FALLS IN POLISH CPI BASKET.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Central Statistical</p>
<p>Office (GUS) reduced the share of food products and boosted the</p>
<p>share of non-food goods in its consumer spending basket used to</p>
<p>calculate the consumer price index, GUS said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>GUS said in a statement that as a result of its annual</p>
<p>household spending survey the structure of the consumer</p>
<p>spending basket was updated as follows:</p>
<p> CONSUMER GOODS	SHARE IN CONSUMER SPENDING BASKET (IN PCT)</p>
<p> AND SERVICES					1996	   1995</p>
<p> Food						 36.85	   39.60</p>
<p> Non-Food Goods				   32.77	   29.79</p>
<p> Alcoholic beverages			     4.00	    4.18</p>
<p> Services					   26.38	   26.43</p>
<p> TOTAL					     100.00	  100.00</p>
<p>GUS, which following the change in the consumer goods and</p>
<p>services basket revised down its January year-on-year inflation</p>
<p>figure to 17.8 percent from earlier announced 18.1 percent,</p>
<p>also released a breakdown of the new revised year-on-year data.</p>
<p>    JANUARY			    yr/yr pct change</p>
<p>    Consumer goods and services   17.8</p>
<p>    Food				  17.9</p>
<p>    Alcoholic beverages	     12.5</p>
<p>    Non-food goods		    16.2</p>
<p>    Services			    20.6</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
